      "source": [
        "***6. Identity Operators*** (is & is not)\n",
        "* The 'is' and 'is not' operator in Python checks whether\n",
        "two variables refer to the exact same object in memory.\n",
        "* It is known as an identity operator."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "N_UhF2zq7N8y",
        "outputId": "b2866bf7-9a7e-4300-df24-7fa001fd764a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "True\n",
            "False\n",
            "True\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# both are used to check if two values are located on same part of the memory\n",
        "\n",
        "a = 20\n",
        "b = 25\n",
        "print(a is not b)\n",
        "print(a is b)\n",
        "\n",
        "b = a\n",
        "print(a is b)\n",
        "\n",
        "# is -> True if the operands are identical\n",
        "# is not -> True if the operands are not identical"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
